f35f932.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued September 25 at 3:41PM MDT until September 25 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...West Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 545 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 341 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nTroublesome Creek, Cub Creek, Bear Creek, North Turkey Creek,\nBlue Creek and Bergen Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to\n0.5 inches are expected over the area. This additional rain will\nresult in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nEvergreen, Kittredge and Wah Keeney Park.","ends":"2026-09-25T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f8253240ab4134ce80abd175e5b3c3719a66d70f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f8253240ab4134ce80abd175e5b3c3719a66d70f.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 3:36PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 336 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from near Rocky Flats to near Tiny Town, or\nextending from 20 miles northwest of Denver to 19 miles southwest of\nDenver, moving east at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nWestern Denver, Lakewood, southwestern Thornton, Arvada,\nWestminster, southwestern Broomfield, northwestern Highlands Ranch,\nLittleton, Northglenn, Englewood, Wheat Ridge, Golden, Federal\nHeights, Sheridan, Morrison, Red Rocks Park, Idledale, Indian Hills\nand Tiny Town.","ends":"2026-09-25T16:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.17d2805fd17238eee5e76607e7dd8a269b5bed8f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.17d2805fd17238eee5e76607e7dd8a269b5bed8f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-25T21:05:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 252105 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 305 PM MDT Fri Sep 25 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another round of showers and isolated storms Friday afternoon and evening. - Drier and warmer this weekend before an upper level trough brings cooler temperatures and potentially our next chances for showers/storms early next week. - Low chances (30%-40%) ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-25T20:58:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight and Saturday...A round of scattered showers and thunderstorms will move east across the plains through this evening. Wetting rains can be expected from most storms. Humidity will be high through tonight, although gusty west winds to around 30 mph will develop over the mountains and higher Front Range Foothills and start to bring in drier air. Saturday will feature warmer and ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"den01","station_name":"Denver","distance_km":21.3,"soil_temp_5cm_f":-999,"soil_temp_15cm_f":-999,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"s